-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":{"constraints":"Add only when Paul never means the heard words literally (nevia → Neyvia). Skip common words (layer, queen, tory) unless Paul asked; the list rewrites every prompt.","options":["add","skip"],"question":"Should these heard words always be written as the name?"},"key":"add-name","section":"judge"}
J add-name add|skip:"Should these heard words always be written as the name?" -- Add only when Paul never means the heard words literally (nevia → Neyvia). Skip common words (layer, queen, tory) unless Paul asked; the list rewrites every prompt.
V J add-name -> human:operator why:"explicit choice required"
-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":{"constraints":"GPU start ~30-55 s, CPU ~3-4 min. Don't poll in a tight loop; check again after the wait, or let Paul's first press record while it loads: the UI holds the whole recording in memory, waits up to 10 min (cancellable) and writes it when the engine is ready.","options":["check-now","later"],"question":"Is the engine likely ready now?"},"key":"engine-wait","section":"judge"}
J engine-wait check-now|later:"Is the engine likely ready now?" -- GPU start ~30-55 s, CPU ~3-4 min. Don't poll in a tight loop; check again after the wait, or let Paul's first press record while it loads: the UI holds the whole recording in memory, waits up to 10 min (cancellable) and writes it when the engine is ready.
V J engine-wait -> human:operator why:"explicit choice required"
-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":{"constraints":"Only Paul decides. \"Send it\" shows a 2 s preview with Stop (Esc); editing the text stops it. A model never sends a dictated prompt on its own.","options":["send","stop"],"question":"Send the dictated prompt?"},"key":"send","section":"judge"}
J send send|stop:"Send the dictated prompt?" -- Only Paul decides. "Send it" shows a 2 s preview with Stop (Esc); editing the text stops it. A model never sends a dictated prompt on its own.
V J send -> human:operator why:"explicit choice required"
-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":{"failure":"French or mixed speech written as English-looking words","recovery":"There is no French speech engine yet: the note says so in plain words (\"Neyvia has no French speech engine on this PC yet, so the English engine wrote its best guess\") with Undo. Check the text or type it; the mic tooltip says English only while status.languages lacks fr"},"key":"0","section":"pitfalls"}
X French or mixed speech written as English-looking words -> There is no French speech engine yet: the note says so in plain words ("Neyvia has no French speech engine on this PC yet, so the English engine wrote its best guess") with Undo. Check the text or type it; the mic tooltip says English only while status.languages lacks fr
-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":{"failure":"Undo says the text changed since","recovery":"Paul typed after the dictation; undo by hand. One-tap Undo only restores an untouched insert"},"key":"1","section":"pitfalls"}
X Undo says the text changed since -> Paul typed after the dictation; undo by hand. One-tap Undo only restores an untouched insert
-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":{"failure":"A command phrase was typed as words","recovery":"undo, cancel and send count only alone or at the end of an utterance; say them after a pause. Test with procedure check-a-command"},"key":"2","section":"pitfalls"}
X A command phrase was typed as words -> undo, cancel and send count only alone or at the end of an utterance; say them after a pause. Test with procedure check-a-command
-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":{"failure":"Mic gives nothing on a phone or another PC","recovery":"The browser mic needs https or localhost: use the :8443 address over Tailscale"},"key":"3","section":"pitfalls"}
X Mic gives nothing on a phone or another PC -> The browser mic needs https or localhost: use the :8443 address over Tailscale
-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":{"failure":"Engine state missing","recovery":"phonon2_engine.py or the dictation Python wasn't found; set engineDir/python in .neyvia/dictation.json via dictation_settings_command"},"key":"4","section":"pitfalls"}
X Engine state missing -> phonon2_engine.py or the dictation Python wasn't found; set engineDir/python in .neyvia/dictation.json via dictation_settings_command
-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":{"failure":"First press after the engine idled out (or while it loads): no grey words","recovery":"Expected: the strip turns amber (\"The speech model is starting. Keep talking\"), every word is held and written once the engine is ready; after release it shows elapsed time and the usual start time. Esc or X drops the recording"},"key":"5","section":"pitfalls"}
X First press after the engine idled out (or while it loads): no grey words -> Expected: the strip turns amber ("The speech model is starting. Keep talking"), every word is held and written once the engine is ready; after release it shows elapsed time and the usual start time. Esc or X drops the recording
-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":{"failure":"Dictation failed after release (backend restarted, engine crashed)","recovery":"The recording stays in memory: the note offers Try again, which waits for the engine and decodes it again. A new dictation replaces it"},"key":"6","section":"pitfalls"}
X Dictation failed after release (backend restarted, engine crashed) -> The recording stays in memory: the note offers Try again, which waits for the engine and decodes it again. A new dictation replaces it
-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":{"failure":"Grey words lag on a CPU engine","recovery":"Partials come every few seconds on CPU; the final text is still complete. Prefer the GPU engine (device cuda)"},"key":"7","section":"pitfalls"}
X Grey words lag on a CPU engine -> Partials come every few seconds on CPU; the final text is still complete. Prefer the GPU engine (device cuda)
-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":"Late re-decode with Qwen needs a local recognizer that accepts PCM (no audio on disk); until one runs, French gets a route_note instead of a rewrite","key":"0","section":"frontier"}
F Late re-decode with Qwen needs a local recognizer that accepts PCM (no audio on disk); until one runs, French gets a route_note instead of a rewrite
-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":"Engine word confidences are not used; stability is agreement between partials plus committed pieces","key":"1","section":"frontier"}
F Engine word confidences are not used; stability is agreement between partials plus committed pieces
-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":"Code dictation (identifiers, symbols) and structural edits beyond the seven commands are not mapped","key":"2","section":"frontier"}
F Code dictation (identifiers, symbols) and structural edits beyond the seven commands are not mapped
-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":"Desktop (Tauri) stream path is wired through the bridge but proven only in the browser so far","key":"3","section":"frontier"}
F Desktop (Tauri) stream path is wired through the bridge but proven only in the browser so far
-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":"A held recording over 28 s is decoded on the one-shot path (no sid), so it cannot get a later French re-decode","key":"4","section":"frontier"}
F A held recording over 28 s is decoded on the one-shot path (no sid), so it cannot get a later French re-decode
-- @record {"chapter":"prompts","data":"The engine's idle timer counts its own load time: with idleExitMinutes shorter than a CPU load it exits before ready (the UI then starts it again)","key":"5","section":"frontier"}
F The engine's idle timer counts its own load time: with idleExitMinutes shorter than a CPU load it exits before ready (the UI then starts it again)
